 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? I'd happily help. Do you want something on big themes of the world, or something on smaller countries you might not have heard of? Then The History of Rome by Mike Duncan is a great place to start. It' gripping and you' finish it in a few weeks. It' very balanced and not sensational. You can follow it with his two seasons on the fall of the Roman Empire if you like. Try 28 Minutes. It' a fast paced tour through history, each episode is about one hour. Enjoy. History is much more fun with friends.",
